-- ============================================================================
-- DR9 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Perforation & Sand Control, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: choosing a completion type from two sieve numbers,
-- Saucier gravel sizing, screen gauge selection, sanding onset from Kirsch
-- stresses at the cavity wall, and walking that onset down an interval.
--
-- THE ENGINE DEFECT THIS TIER TEACHES, AND IT IS THE POINT OF MODULE 5.
-- cdpAlongInterval walked its sweep under a `md <= bottomMdM` loop guard, which
-- exits before the clamp inside the loop can fire. On any interval whose step
-- does not divide it evenly the deepest metres were never screened at all. On
-- an interval whose base is the weak rock, that is the row that GOVERNS, and
-- dropping it flips the reported margin positive. It was invisible on every
-- interval whose step happened to divide it, which is every interval anybody
-- had written a fixture for.
--
-- WHY THE GOLDEN COULD NOT SEE IT, WHICH IS THE LESSON WORTH MORE THAN THE BUG.
-- The fixture exercised only the evenly dividing case, and the oracle
-- TRANSCRIBED THE ENGINE'S OWN LOOP rather than deriving the stations it should
-- visit. An oracle that reproduces the implementation reproduces its mistakes,
-- and it will agree with the engine precisely where the engine is wrong. The
-- fix therefore came with four guards and not one: an engine test, a ragged
-- golden case whose step does not divide its interval, an oracle that now walks
-- an EXPLICIT station list, and an app-level guard on the step.
--
-- THE TIER'S OTHER STANDING HABIT: check both ends of anything that walks a
-- range. The governing row of a sweep is a minimum over rows, and a minimum is
-- a REDUCTION over data rather than data. Verifying the rows does not verify
-- the reduction, which is the same lesson DR8 paid for in a different engine.
--
-- WHAT THE TIER REFUSES. The sanding calculation is an ONSET criterion. It says
-- when the cavity wall begins to fail and it says nothing whatever about how
-- much sand follows, at what rate, or for how long. A margin is not a rate, and
-- the lessons decline to turn one into the other.
-- ============================================================================

values ('perfsand', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-choosing-a-completion-type","title":"Choosing a Completion Type","lesson_keys":["l01-the-question-the-sieve-answers","l02-the-ladder","l03-fines-decide-the-middle","l04-what-a-screening-rule-is-worth"]},{"key":"m02-gravel","title":"Gravel","lesson_keys":["l01-saucier","l02-the-band-is-narrow","l03-when-nothing-matches","l04-the-nearest-sand","l05-why-five-to-six"]},{"key":"m03-screens","title":"Screens","lesson_keys":["l01-the-gravel-pack-rule","l02-a-gauge-series-is-not-continuous","l03-standalone-and-the-coberly-window","l04-the-margin-you-actually-get","l05-what-a-screen-does-not-do"]},{"key":"m04-sanding-onset","title":"Sanding Onset","lesson_keys":["l01-kirsch-at-the-cavity-wall","l02-the-critical-flowing-pressure","l03-two-cavity-geometries","l04-the-strength-boost-factor","l05-a-margin-not-a-sand-rate"]},{"key":"m05-the-sweep-and-the-missing-row","title":"The Sweep, and the Missing Row","lesson_keys":["l01-walking-the-interval","l02-the-row-that-was-never-computed","l03-why-the-golden-could-not-see-it","l04-what-the-fix-asserts"]},{"key":"m06-the-expert-reading","title":"The Expert Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
